{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/932708-the-scion-ichor-viel","id":932708,"title":"The Scion/Ichor Viel?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-16T18:05:29-07:00","id":932708,"title":"The Scion/Ichor Viel?","content":"What is the limit of people being able to see the supernatural in Scion?<br /> <br /> Some of the giants etc have clearly described differences between what mortals see and what a scion/something with legend sees. Is this ever clearly defined?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T18:22:55-07:00","id":932715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Viovode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/932708-the-scion-ichor-viel#post932708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the limit of people being able to see the supernatural in Scion?<br /> <br /> Some of the giants etc have clearly described differences between what mortals see and what a scion/something with legend sees. Is this ever clearly defined?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's somewhat odd. Some supernaturals, like those Giants you mention, have details written about having something like a veil. Pretty much nothing else does. There is no difference in 99% of the cases that divide what mortals and people with Legend Dots see. I think that clause with some of the Giants is a vestigial rule left over from a very early idea that was never worked in to the game.<br /> <br /> Outside of people using the Illusion Purview, or who are Supernaturally good at disguise (Manannan, Odin, Radegast, ect) Mortals see everything just as it is. When Apollo is walking around as a Legend 12 God in New York City, everyone sees him, and adores him with every fiber of their being for example. There is no Masquerade in Scion, either socially enforced, or enforced by Fate. But, those Giant entries really are a source of confusion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:47:05-07:00","id":932742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted Viovode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/932708-the-scion-ichor-viel#post932708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the limit of people being able to see the supernatural in Scion?<br /> <br /> Some of the giants etc have clearly described differences between what mortals see and what a scion/something with legend sees. Is this ever clearly defined?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't think there's any actual limit to it, per say. The fear of mortals seeing you in action is less about blowing your cover, and more about the possibility of Fate Bonds. There are several references that mention if a mortal sees you using some kind of overtly divine power, they become bound to you, and the worst Fate Bonds can survive even after death.<br /> <br /> So to avoid the possibility of getting roped into something you don't want to be / do, it's best to keep a low profile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T20:20:20-07:00","id":932759,"title":"","content":"I just double checked Scion: Hero, and I'm unsure Fatebindings have anything to do with how overtly you are flashing your skills. On page 222, it outlines using legend to reroll, using legend on any Boon or Knack, or using a Magic Boon. Nothing at all to do with being witnessed specifically being the problematic part. Being seen doing Divine things doesn't have any effect on a Scion or God, but spending legend does.<br /> <br /> For example, if someone has made themselves invisible with Darkness, Illusion, or Moon, and then they cause an Earthquake with Earth, even though no one witnessed them doing so, they would provoke Fatebindings. Keeping a low profile, in RAW, doesn't do anything to your capacity to develop Fatebindings <i>except</i> that it prevents you from gaining Legend Dots in RAW as they are specifically bound to your fame/infamy. Higher your Legend Dots, easier it is to be Fatebound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T21:17:49-07:00","id":932780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/932708-the-scion-ichor-viel?p=932759#post932759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just double checked Scion: Hero, and I'm unsure Fatebindings have anything to do with how overtly you are flashing your skills. On page 222, it outlines using legend to reroll, using legend on any Boon or Knack, or using a Magic Boon. Nothing at all to do with being witnessed specifically being the problematic part. Being seen doing Divine things doesn't have any effect on a Scion or God, but spending legend does.<br /> <br /> For example, if someone has made themselves invisible with Darkness, Illusion, or Moon, and then they cause an Earthquake with Earth, even though no one witnessed them doing so, they would provoke Fatebindings. Keeping a low profile, in RAW, doesn't do anything to your capacity to develop Fatebindings <i>except</i> that it prevents you from gaining Legend Dots in RAW as they are specifically bound to your fame/infamy. Higher your Legend Dots, easier it is to be Fatebound.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I thought some of the higher level Boons (Demigod / God level) say that they immediately Fatebind any mortals who witness them.<br /> <br /> Unless I misunderstood how that works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T22:14:48-07:00","id":932788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/932708-the-scion-ichor-viel?p=932780#post932780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought some of the higher level Boons (Demigod / God level) say that they immediately Fatebind any mortals who witness them.<br /> <br /> Unless I misunderstood how that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know The Best Trick does something sort of like that. I think you get Fatebound to anyone who you directly save due to the intervention of your illusion. I checked God and Demigod, but couldn't see anything at a glance. But, while I can't find anything that says that, at the same time there could be rules somewhere else saying otherwise. You know what the RAW Fate stuff is like, all over the place and never particularly clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}